  "book_id": "6953cbb777f38f6761bdfc4d",
  "reason": "The draft does not transcribe this leaf; it supplies a different Greek text of Judges xi.34–xii.12 (for example \"ΕΜΠΕΠΛΕΚΕΣ ΜΕ ΚΑΙ ΣΥ ΕΓΕΝΟΥ\" where the page shows \"ΕΜΠΕΠΟΔΟΣΤΑΤΗΚΑΣ ΜΕ\", and it leaves out the \"ΕΤΑΠΕΙΝΟΥΝ ΜΕ\" that opens the right column), and this faded, blotted facsimile, with its struck-through lines, is too degraded to transcribe reliably line by line."
 },
 {
  "id": "opus:69938e3bd5a98fd66f430f3e",
  "judged_as": null,
  "cell": "greek-flash3/unknown",
  "route": "opus",
  "kind": "contain",
  "page_id": "69938e3bd5a98fd66f430f3e",
  "book_id": "69938e3bd5a98fd66f430e65",
  "reason": "The draft does not match this leaf: it is invented philosophical prose about daemons, virtue and Helenos, while the image is a two-page spread of a Greek manuscript about Mantinea and the Lacedaemonians (Agesipolis, Philip, Antigonus), with folio number 207 and different marginal notes."
 },
