  "reason": "The draft is an invention, not this leaf's text: the image is a two-page spread (folio 207) of a Greek handwritten Pausanias on Mantineia (Lacedaemonians, Mantineans, Antigonus, Philip son of Perseus, Asklepios, Praxiteles, Gryllos son of Xenophon), whereas the draft gives a fabricated philosophical discourse on daemons and virtue, labelled Plotinus, that matches the page in neither its lines nor its marginal notes."
